{
  "id": "COMPOUND:15637 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Oleiferin C appears to have a shared target of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A and Cyclizidine, all of which ultimately lead to VMRC-MELG. This suggests a potential pathway where Oleiferin C may modulate the activity of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and thus influence VMRC-MELG through a common intermediate. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, each linking Oleiferin C to VMRC-MELG via different targets, reinforcing the possibility of a broader, interconnected mechanism. The reliance on Thioredoxin, mitochondrial as a central node highlights a recurring role in the pathway, potentially involving redox regulation or protein interaction. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Oleiferin C may exert its effects through a mechanism involving Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and ultimately VMRC-MELG, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
